# Lab Local DNS records — git-tracked source of truth for pihole Local DNS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Format: "<IP>  <hostname>" (one per line) — matches pihole v6
# /etc/pihole/hosts/custom.list and the Settings → Local DNS Records UI.
#
# WHY: gives every infra host a stable .lab name independent of the router's
# cosmetic client labels (Deco names are cosmetic; Archer/OPNsense later).
# Seeded from docs/deco-device-naming.md (fixed-MAC infra only — MAC-randomized
# phones/tablets/IoT omitted, their IPs drift).
#
# APPLY (pihole @ 192.168.68.248):
#   1. UI: Settings → Local DNS Records → add each line, OR
#   2. CLI: copy these lines into /etc/pihole/hosts/custom.list then
#      `pihole reloaddns` (or restart FTL). Back up the file first.
# After applying: `dig book5.lab @192.168.68.248 +short` → 192.168.68.250
#
# Keep this file in sync when IPs change. Pair with DHCP reservations once
# pihole owns DHCP (Archer DHCP off — Phase 2.0) so IP == name == lease.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Proxmox / infra
192.168.68.250  book5.lab
192.168.68.249  tower.lab
192.168.68.248  pihole.lab

# VMs
192.168.68.100  omarchy.lab
192.168.68.101  ubuntu.lab
192.168.68.111  home-assistant.lab
192.168.68.111  ha.lab

# Containers / appliances
192.168.68.61   homelable.lab

# Cameras (Frigate on VM101)
192.168.68.75   petcam.lab
192.168.68.76   porch.lab

# Gateway (Deco now / Archer after Friday 2026-06-26 cutover — IP unchanged .1)
192.168.68.1    gateway.lab

# Trusted client (wife laptop — pihole bypass group; real MAC, won't rotate)
192.168.68.59   wife-laptop.lab
